# server/.dockerignore
#
# Tells Docker which files to exclude when copying into the image.
# Works exactly like .gitignore but for Docker's COPY instruction.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS:
# Without .dockerignore, "COPY . ." in the Dockerfile copies EVERYTHING
# including node_modules (potentially hundreds of MB), .env files with
# real secrets, and test files that don't belong in a production image.
# .dockerignore keeps the build context small (faster builds) and the
# image clean (no accidentally leaked secrets).

# Dependencies — these get reinstalled inside the container via npm ci.
# Never copy host node_modules into an image — platform-specific binaries
# compiled on your Windows machine won't run on the Alpine Linux container.
node_modules/

# Compiled output — the builder stage compiles fresh inside the container.
dist/

# Environment files — secrets must come from environment variables
# injected at runtime (docker-compose, Railway, etc), never baked
# into the image itself. An image with a real .env could be pushed
# to a registry and expose credentials to anyone who pulls it.
.env
.env.*

# Test files — don't belong in a production image.
# Tests run in CI (GitHub Actions), not inside the deployed container.
src/**/__tests__/
src/**/*.test.ts
vitest.config.ts

# Development-only files
*.md
.gitignore